cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software, please cite it.
title: "HPC Chaperone: separate identities for AI agents on shared HPC systems"
abstract: >-
  Runs AI coding agents, tools, scripts and Slurm jobs on an HPC cluster as a
  per-user persona: a real directory user created on first launch, with its own
  HOME, the human's environment, the human's groups minus banned ones, and its
  own Slurm account. Built from FreeIPA, SSSD, Slurm, sudo and Unix groups; one
  Go binary, no daemon. A separate identity, not a sandbox.
type: software
